WEBVTT

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:20.410
"Traveling Former Baker Assistant
Tells You All About Yeast"

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:24.540
"195: Traveling Former Baker Assistant
I'm in Kagawa now.
Udon is the best food man's ever made."

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:26.290
"196: Anonymous
Oh, you're in Shikoku?"

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:26.290
"197: Udon Territory."

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:28.410
"359: Traveling Former Baker Assistant
Okay, today I'll tell you
how I left the bread factory."

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:29.950
"You guys know what's up
with the factory, right?"

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:33.250
"Huh?"

00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:33.250
"The Former Baker's catchphrase."

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:33.250
"(ASSISTANT) baker."

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.250
"Tell us, Assistant!"

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:35.700
"360: Traveling Former Baker Assistant
Okay. Man you guys are greedy."

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:38.160
"61: Traveling Former Baker Assistant
Okay, here I go."

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.660
Delicious, piping hot elephants!

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:45.270
"Kitty-Made Bakery"

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:46.000
In the darkness of the bread factory,
where countless bacteria dwell,

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.700
you'll find six bakers.

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:49.270
"Bean Jam Bun"

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:50.120
Bean Jam Bun. White Bread.

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:50.070
"White Bread"

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:50.900
"Curry Bread"

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:53.370
Curry Bread! When you bite in,
will you taste butter, or jam?

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:51.780
"Pig in a Blanket"

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:52.690
"Triple Bun"

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:53.400
"Churros"

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:58.330
Behold this battle of wheats between bakers!

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:02.790
Christmas, one month ago.

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:11.250
Following Champee's orders,
the bakers were able to stop the bomber.

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:13.590
"Dog"

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:13.580
You know that already, right?

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:19.890
"Yeah, we heard."

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:19.890
"The three bakers, right?"

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:19.890
"Dork... Virgin... Failed Dick."

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:25.120
Champee's my boss, by the way.

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:32.200
What? He's talking about us.

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:29.810
"The Comedian Baker."
"The pervert baker."

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:33.040
Right?

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:36.000
I happened to see it, so I came to tell you.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.790
I'm so smart!

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:41.410
His boss is the Comedian Baker Champee.

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:44.450
The one who's writing this can't be...

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:46.870
Watson- <i>san</i> , right?

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:50.250
He just vanished with no warning,

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:52.500
made us worry...

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.370
And now he's off eating udon?

00:01:55.370 --> 00:01:58.830
I'm glad, though, that he's doing well...

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:04.540
Mrs. Hudson, isn't this...?

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:10.160
And so I left the bakery without coming back.

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:13.080
Because it's my fault that Forest...

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:14.830
Forest?

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:16.910
He must mean Moriarty.

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:18.700
James.

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:24.790
I got between Champee and Forest.

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:26.790
And that's why it all happened.

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:30.160
--This way!
--Find him!

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:49.410
Champee...

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:26.820
"The Thread Where We Talk About Yeast"

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:29.950
Just give it a try!

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:32.080
Your skin's a mess!

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:35.580
Here, put it on your cute little wiener, too!

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:37.660
It'll be nice and smooth in two seconds flat!

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:44.830
Sherlock...

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:51.200
I got a call from Mrs. Hudson
and came to see you.

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:53.660
She said you've had a bad time.

00:04:57.910 --> 00:05:01.450
I guess you can't get a hold of Watson either.

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:06.250
Hey, Sherlock.

00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:09.700
I know you're shocked about
what happened with Moriarty.

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:11.370
"Sher"

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:17.920
"Sher"

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:25.000
Well?

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:27.700
I see.

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:29.580
What about the others?

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:30.950
They doing okay?

00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:36.540
They stopped coming. Everybody
split up after what happened.

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:41.290
They haven't found it yet, huh?

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:47.950
"James Moran's Body Remains Missing"

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:49.160
Moriarty...

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:52.580
I don't want to hear that name.

00:05:56.450 --> 00:05:59.700
Diana is...

00:06:02.830 --> 00:06:06.580
So Tora- <i>chan</i> went off to find Diana on his own.

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:07.540
Well?

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:10.450
Why not join in, get a change of scenery?

00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:15.250
Anyway, I'll tell you what's up, I guess.

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:21.910
Last night, Chinkill and Diana
got picked up by two men.

00:06:21.910 --> 00:06:25.500
They hit it off and went to a hotel.

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:27.790
And then all of a sudden...

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:29.700
This is the police! Hands up!

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:34.250
The two men were actually
serial killers who would

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:33.700
"Escapee From 7th Prison"

00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:35.740
"Escapee From 7th Prison"

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:37.160
murder their partners during intercourse.

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:41.370
And escapees from 7th prison, too!

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:49.200
The police are searching
for Diana and the escaped man,

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:53.250
but there're no clues, and the
investigation isn't going well.

00:06:53.250 --> 00:06:56.830
The man who was arrested
bit clean through his tongue

00:06:56.830 --> 00:06:59.750
and killed himself before he could be interrogated.

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:02.660
There's one strange thing though.

00:07:02.660 --> 00:07:05.080
Before he died the man read a string of numbers:

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:08.830
8020463840.

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:11.750
Sherlock?

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:16.540
Moriarty's alive!

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:18.620
"Sher"

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:20.450
Hey, Sherlock!

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:24.370
Christ!

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:26.120
Right now I'm in Okinawa.

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:28.000
The sea's so blue.

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:31.580
Sata Andagi is a really
hard word to say, you know.

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:33.580
S'all good.

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:34.790
You're a free spirit, Assistant!

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:37.080
I wish I could be like you!

00:07:34.790 --> 00:07:37.080
Man, I wish I was an assistant!

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:39.750
No, my life is shit.

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:42.120
Okay, now I'll tell you about me.

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:43.410
Oh, good stuff!

00:07:43.410 --> 00:07:45.790
The story of the assistant's life!

00:07:45.910 --> 00:07:50.610
"Tea Field Incident"

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:48.540
I grew up in Shizuoka.

00:07:48.540 --> 00:07:51.870
My family are, typically enough, tea farmers.

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:55.410
You're so nice, John.

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:58.040
Thanks for always helping, John!

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:04.200
I was a really good kid.

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:06.500
But one day...

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:08.200
John, what's wrong?

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:11.080
What's with the mattress?

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:13.950
Daddy's playing pro wrestling!

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:22.950
Dad, I brought you a mattress!

00:08:22.950 --> 00:08:24.290
Use this!

00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:26.580
John, what are you doing here?

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:33.620
God damn!

00:08:33.620 --> 00:08:36.580
Of course, I didn't know any better.

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:43.330
A few months later, my parents divorced.

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:46.580
The last words my dad told me were...

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:51.260
"It's your fault the family's ruined."

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:53.620
"The Lunch Incident"

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:55.910
Typically enough,

00:08:55.910 --> 00:08:59.370
my teacher in middle school
wouldn't let you not eat your lunch.

00:09:01.370 --> 00:09:03.500
I'll eat it for you.

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:18.160
That simple action brought out
the selfish side of the class.

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:24.160
"Maki Maki" "Stupid Stupid"

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:22.870
Of course, I didn't mean anything by it.

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:28.580
"It's your fault the class is ruined."

00:09:28.660 --> 00:09:31.340
"The Germ Incident"

00:09:31.620 --> 00:09:36.160
Things were going well
when I got my start as a Baker.

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:40.410
Work and well, women...

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:44.040
This was the first time
in my life I was popular.

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:46.580
But a problem happened soon after.

00:09:50.910 --> 00:09:54.160
They all fought over me...

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:55.750
You guys get it, right?

00:09:55.750 --> 00:10:00.580
I always ruin whatever environment I'm in.

00:10:00.580 --> 00:10:05.620
Yes. I am...

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:05.660
"You're a germ."

00:10:06.120 --> 00:10:07.660
And...

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:14.300
"The Bakery Incident"

00:10:15.450 --> 00:10:17.700
Sherlock!

00:10:20.950 --> 00:10:26.370
Moriarty!

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:26.370
Then I did it again.

00:10:26.370 --> 00:10:30.250
I'm a wrecker.

00:10:30.250 --> 00:10:32.950
Wherever I go, it doesn't change.

00:10:32.950 --> 00:10:35.200
It's better I'm not around.

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:36.750
So I left on a journey.

00:10:36.750 --> 00:10:39.950
8020463840...

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:43.250
Hold it!

00:10:43.250 --> 00:10:44.540
Hide your floppy wiener!

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:45.200
"Sher"

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:49.450
--Why's he naked?
--Jeez...

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:54.450
Found him, Irene!

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:00.750
Hey, old man.

00:11:00.750 --> 00:11:02.700
You around?

00:11:04.660 --> 00:11:08.250
You're hiding from me, huh?

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:12.080
Sherlock...

00:11:12.080 --> 00:11:14.870
You can be a jerk sometimes, old man.

00:11:14.870 --> 00:11:16.830
You're hiding back there, right?

00:11:16.830 --> 00:11:19.410
Come on out, damn it!

00:11:21.830 --> 00:11:24.750
Let's go home, Sherlock.

00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:30.950
That's <i>Koheiji the Living</i> , right?

00:11:30.950 --> 00:11:36.000
The tempo, the rhythm... I like your <i>rakugo</i> .

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:42.160
Why not be a detective?

00:11:47.370 --> 00:11:51.290
Hey, why don't we get out
of Kabukicho for a while?

00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:54.580
I'll take you anywhere you want to go.

00:11:54.580 --> 00:11:55.910
How about it?

00:11:55.910 --> 00:12:00.700
I mean mystery-solving <i>rakugo</i> ...

00:12:01.790 --> 00:12:03.700
Sherlock.

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:09.330
Moriarty is dead.

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:15.920
"Sher"

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:21.500
I can't do it on my own, can I?

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:36.080
Help me. I want to save Sherlock.

00:12:45.500 --> 00:12:47.620
Shikoku? Okinawa?

00:12:47.620 --> 00:12:51.000
You haven't gone anywhere except your fantasies!

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:57.540
I can't...

00:12:57.540 --> 00:12:59.540
I can't do anything!

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:02.250
Huh? What's going on?

00:13:02.250 --> 00:13:03.700
What's happening?

00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:05.450
A fight?

00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:09.620
You saw the messages from Mrs. Hudson, right?

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:13.750
You're the only one who can
bring him to his senses!

00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:17.160
Leave, please.

00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:20.290
You changed Sherlock!

00:13:22.750 --> 00:13:28.500
But your naivety is a bad influence on Sherlock.

00:13:28.500 --> 00:13:29.870
Yes.

00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:32.830
That's why he died.

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:36.660
I'm sorry, Moriarty!

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:42.200
I'm disappointed in you.

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:45.580
Say whatever you want!

00:13:45.580 --> 00:13:46.700
Shut up.

00:13:46.700 --> 00:13:47.870
Get lost, scum.

00:13:47.870 --> 00:13:49.500
God, what a nuisance.

00:13:49.500 --> 00:13:51.660
What a pain!

00:13:57.160 --> 00:13:59.660
Okay, we're done.

00:13:59.660 --> 00:14:02.700
It's hard to investigate
without clothing, right?

00:14:07.120 --> 00:14:09.370
And...

00:14:09.370 --> 00:14:11.160
I'll go with you!

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:12.700
I'll help you.

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:16.080
Keep looking until you're satisfied.

00:14:29.120 --> 00:14:31.370
Seriously? You've seen him?

00:14:33.450 --> 00:14:36.290
This is one of the escaped prisoners?

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:40.120
Yeah. One of the remaining three.

00:14:40.120 --> 00:14:42.000
I know where he is!

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:43.750
Under the bridge on 3rd avenue!

00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:46.330
I can't believe you remembered that!

00:14:46.330 --> 00:14:47.500
It's a big help.

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:50.290
Share this with the others.

00:14:51.580 --> 00:14:53.450
Hey, Sherlock!

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:56.580
It was worth doing all that work.

00:14:56.580 --> 00:14:57.950
Time to...

00:14:57.950 --> 00:14:59.540
What?

00:15:16.160 --> 00:15:19.430
"7th Prison Escapee"

00:15:27.750 --> 00:15:29.080
I found him.

00:15:29.080 --> 00:15:30.250
That's Sherlock.

00:15:30.250 --> 00:15:33.080
And a woman named Irene is with him.

00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:35.080
Okay, watch them.

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:37.540
Watch? Why don't you arrest him already?

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:43.370
Even if he was in contact with Moriarty...
I mean James Moran.

00:15:43.370 --> 00:15:46.700
Sherlock hasn't committed any crimes yet!

00:15:54.330 --> 00:15:58.540
Thinking back, ever since I met Champee...

00:16:02.790 --> 00:16:06.330
I might've changed.

00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:10.830
Everything was so crazy ever since
I became an assistant baker.

00:16:10.830 --> 00:16:13.870
I was surrounded by weirdos.

00:16:13.870 --> 00:16:16.540
It was crazy, but...

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:22.830
They made me forget that
I'm a germ who ruins everything.

00:16:24.450 --> 00:16:26.830
Yes! Future!

00:16:26.830 --> 00:16:28.750
Future!

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:32.080
For the first time, I was able to be somewhere

00:16:32.080 --> 00:16:34.750
without thinking I needed to leave.

00:16:39.620 --> 00:16:43.870
But... I made everything go crazy,

00:16:43.870 --> 00:16:47.700
even Champee.

00:16:47.700 --> 00:16:50.370
And because of that, Forest...

00:16:54.120 --> 00:16:58.580
I don't want to cause any
more problems for Champee.

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:01.370
It's starting.

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:03.330
He's different than usual.

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:04.500
What happened?

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:06.620
Some kind of love triangle.

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:08.250
When do we talk about yeast?

00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:10.250
"Kaneko Financing"

00:17:10.910 --> 00:17:13.000
Oh, Doctor.

00:17:14.580 --> 00:17:17.330
Boss Kaneko.

00:17:17.330 --> 00:17:20.660
Sounds like you've had a rough time of it.

00:17:20.660 --> 00:17:22.370
Yes, I guess.

00:17:22.370 --> 00:17:25.290
Sherlock's in a bad way--

00:17:23.830 --> 00:17:25.290
I'm sorry.

00:17:25.290 --> 00:17:27.950
I'm in a hurry, so I'll be going.

00:17:27.950 --> 00:17:30.040
Doctor...

00:17:30.040 --> 00:17:36.370
That weirdo changed a little
since you came, Doctor.

00:17:38.700 --> 00:17:45.370
Like a <i>rakugo</i> -loving robot
became a <i>rakugo</i> -loving bratty kid.

00:17:45.370 --> 00:17:52.200
So I don't want you to give up on him.

00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:54.200
Please.

00:18:01.370 --> 00:18:05.540
If you don't stop him,
Champee will become Forest.

00:18:05.540 --> 00:18:08.830
He needs his assistant.

00:18:08.830 --> 00:18:11.160
From Airi Version 0.0.

00:18:13.790 --> 00:18:16.120
You okay?

00:18:16.120 --> 00:18:19.290
Yes. I'm sorry.

00:18:19.290 --> 00:18:22.330
I just got a little dizzy.

00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:24.080
Thank you.

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:25.620
Not at all...

00:18:31.120 --> 00:18:34.910
I got pickpocketed again.

00:18:34.910 --> 00:18:36.080
Hey!

00:18:36.080 --> 00:18:38.000
What are you laughing at?

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:40.540
You're so stupid.

00:18:40.540 --> 00:18:43.040
Get used to this town already.

00:18:49.410 --> 00:18:53.450
Even if it's you, Sherlock... I'll get mad!

00:18:53.450 --> 00:18:56.580
It's okay, right?

00:18:56.580 --> 00:18:58.410
Believe in me.

00:19:16.250 --> 00:19:18.290
I finally understand.

00:19:21.580 --> 00:19:23.370
Follow Sherlock!

00:19:24.910 --> 00:19:31.370
I changed Champee and ruined
things between him and Forest.

00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:33.200
But...

00:19:33.200 --> 00:19:39.330
Maybe I was the one who kept him in this world.

00:19:39.330 --> 00:19:40.620
--Did you find him?
--No.

00:19:40.620 --> 00:19:42.160
We lost him!

00:19:42.160 --> 00:19:43.580
--Where is he?
--Find him!

00:19:43.580 --> 00:19:45.540
We can't find him!

00:19:45.540 --> 00:19:47.500
Champee is...

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:51.870
...at a crossroads right now.

00:19:54.870 --> 00:19:57.870
He's a strange, strange man.

00:20:01.660 --> 00:20:05.160
Selfish. A jerk.

00:20:07.330 --> 00:20:09.580
And he eats really weird food.

00:20:11.290 --> 00:20:15.000
But he's my friend.

00:20:18.500 --> 00:20:21.000
Champee believed in me.

00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:24.870
You're a fool. And a good guy.

00:20:31.450 --> 00:20:33.000
So...

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:40.500
I'll believe in Champee.

00:20:40.500 --> 00:20:42.080
No matter what!

00:20:44.080 --> 00:20:45.870
I'll save him!

00:20:48.750 --> 00:20:52.830
Everybody, I'm sorry we're
not talking about yeast.

00:20:52.830 --> 00:20:56.620
I'm on Shinjuku's east side right now.

00:20:58.080 --> 00:21:00.000
Kabukicho.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:03.330
I've finally found my town.

00:21:08.080 --> 00:21:09.370
I...

00:21:10.370 --> 00:21:12.910
I...

00:21:17.750 --> 00:21:20.660
I'm not a baker's assistant.

00:21:23.370 --> 00:21:26.660
I'm the assistant of Sherlock Holmes,
the great detective!

00:21:28.250 --> 00:21:29.870
Sherlock!

00:21:37.290 --> 00:21:40.040
Um... I...

00:21:40.040 --> 00:21:42.250
I want to start over--

00:23:45.060 --> 00:23:50.070
"Everybody Be There At Eight"

00:23:45.290 --> 00:23:48.040
Moriarty's alive...

00:23:50.070 --> 00:23:52.070
"Tony Shigeru is Type AB"
"Today's Poem: I love Washlets - Shigeru"
"Tony faces his greatest peril!"
"A slump!"
